# Copy to CODEOWNERS (or .github/CODEOWNERS), replace @your-org/platform with the people who own the harness, and turn on
# "Require review from Code Owners" for the branch. These are the files that decide what a change is judged by, so a PR may not
# loosen them on its own say-so; the per-change state under .rig/changes/ is not here, so ordinary work needs no owner review.
# scripts/owners.spec.ts keeps this list equal to the harness-tamper sensor's protected paths, no wider and no narrower.
/.rig/sensors.json                @your-org/platform
/.rig/rules.json                  @your-org/platform
/.rig/ratchets.json               @your-org/platform
/.rig/layers.approved.json        @your-org/platform
/.rig/gen/                        @your-org/platform
/.rig/verify/                     @your-org/platform
/.rig/lessons.md                  @your-org/platform
/.rig/lessons-archive.md          @your-org/platform
/.rig/guides/                     @your-org/platform
/.rig/evals/                      @your-org/platform
/.rig/bin/                        @your-org/platform
/.rig/mod/                        @your-org/platform
/.rig/githooks/                   @your-org/platform
/.claude-plugin/                  @your-org/platform
/.claude/                         @your-org/platform
/CLAUDE.md                        @your-org/platform
/.github/workflows/rig-*.yml      @your-org/platform
/.github/workflows/sdlc-check.yml @your-org/platform
/CODEOWNERS                       @your-org/platform
/.github/CODEOWNERS               @your-org/platform
# The waiver ledger is evidence a person adds to; CI already wants an independent reviewer for new rows.
/.rig/waivers.jsonl               @your-org/platform
